area the  thing about it though is that this is  not supposed to be a realistic golf area  city if it were I probably just be  recreating Dubai or Doha and leave it at  that but it's actually more of like  fantasy plan about how I would see that  goal cities could be built or should be  built  maybe if there would be better cities to  live in so it's not as much a project  where I'm trying to create something  really realistic but more kind of an  idealistic thing almost where I'm trying  to create the perfect city which there  is no way that you can create the  perfect city but that's that's much more  close to what I'm trying to do here it's  basically a kind of a prototype of what  I think core cities should look like  if there would be cities that I would  love to live in and think would be just  nice places in general and the fact that  it looks a bit European and not so golf  area ish is probably a result of that  and the fact that I'm just European I'm  probably not going to be able to like  get rid of every trace of the way that I  think cities work but really that's just  the reason I think many of these cities  like to buy and Doha even though there's  such modern bland cities they still  cling to these like 60s ideals of very  cars centric layouts and that's the one  thing that I wanted to fix mostly with  the city and actually make a city that's  at least somewhat walkable as much as it  can be in this kind of area and focus on  public transport and on making  pedestrian friendly areas as well and  just in general kind of making a city  where I would think I yeah I would kind  of like to live there so really that's  just a plan it's it's not as much  focused on realism it's also not as much  focused on the skyline of the city or  the look of it it's really just focused  on really I would say almost the social  dimension of how it would be to live  there so yeah that's really just what I  wanted to say about that and for me  sustainability also plays a role in it's  just because more and more people are  gonna live in cities and I think it's  just really interesting to think about  how you can make cities more sustainable  for not just nature but also the people  that live in it and I think it's a good  time to also start thinking about how we  can make cities better and a game which  is pretty much this the sandbox to go  loose with your wildest fantasies about  city building feels like just about the  perfect place in which you can do so and  city skylines is definitely the first  game in which you can do that with this  amount of control so that's really  what's been motivating me and if we're  hit to get back on topic very quickly  this is the marina area instead of using  a key here I actually figured let's go  back to a workshop I set because there  is only a straight section and a curve  that could sort of curves the inside so  I wouldn't have any issues with like  curve  that aren't as smooth as the key curves  and it's just a little bit nicer because  it also comes with some benches and some  planters and a nice big texture on the  side so hopefully that can be turned  into a pretty fancy marina at some point  in the future it's not going to be a  very big marina I also do want to have a  couple of those in the future but  especially right now in many of these  Gulf cities marinas are sprawl  throughout the cities and quite a big  thing and this is the only one that the  central island is going to have so I  better turn it into something that's  worthwhile also a very quick note you  can still see all of the cars using the  pedestrian paths which is annoying for a  couple of reasons they should be there  in the first place but also they're kind  of going through everything biding over  the basketball courts and running  through trees and stuff like that which  is annoying as hell I hope to fix that  in the future  I actually got Traffic Manager President  edition instead of the one which I had  before which was Traffic Manager plus AI  and with that you can actually block  certain vehicles from going on certain  roads I just haven't done it yet because  it's gonna take a lot of work and right  now I'd rather just focus on the way  that the city looks and just take some  boring time off in which I'm otherwise  not doing anything to fix the cars going  over roads but I'm super annoyed by it  as well just wanted to say that and I'm  looking into fixing it in the future  it's just sort of something to stick up  with right now as the city or at least  the central island isn't completely  finished but it's it's something to work  on definitely anyway that is just about  it for this time apps the central island  of the city is pretty much finished at  this point I might come back to it at  some point in the future and do some  finishing touches and maybe come back to  some things that I end up not liking as  much as I initially thought you know  it's really hard to say when something  is really finished but this is finished  to the point where I feel safe moving on  to other areas and start laying out the  rest of the city so that's what we're  going to do in the next episode I'm not  sure which part I'm going to tackle yet  but we're going to get into the other  and some of the I would call almost  suburbs of the city at least not the  complete Central Island and see how  we're going to make those so thank you  guys for watching and I hope to see you  guys next time
 

